1
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:59,793
A Jedi shall not know anger. Nor hatred. Nor love.

2
00:09:47,586 --> 00:09:53,586
Star Wars: Episode II - Attack of the Clones is a adventure,
action, science fiction film directed by George Lucas.

3
00:14:41,379 --> 00:14:47,379
Following an assassination attempt on Senator Padmé Amidala, Jedi Knights Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi
investigate a mysterious plot into the heart of the Separatist movement and the beginning of the Clone Wars.

4
00:19:35,172 --> 00:19:41,172
Anakin Skywalker, played by Hayden Christensen.

5
00:24:28,965 --> 00:24:34,965
Obi-Wan Kenobi, played by Ewan McGregor.

6
00:29:22,758 --> 00:29:28,758
Padmé Amidala, played by Natalie Portman.

7
00:34:16,551 --> 00:34:22,551
Count Dooku, played by Christopher Lee.

8
00:39:10,344 --> 00:39:16,344
Mace Windu, played by Samuel L. Jackson.

9
00:44:04,137 --> 00:44:10,137
Yoda (voice), played by Frank Oz.

10
00:48:57,931 --> 00:49:03,931
Star Wars: Attack of the Clones (also known as Star Wars: Episode II – Attack of the Clones) is a 2002 American
epic space opera film directed by George Lucas from a screenplay he co-wrote with Jonathan Hales.

11
00:53:51,724 --> 00:53:57,724
The sequel to The Phantom Menace (1999), it is the fifth entry in the Star Wars
film series and second chronological chapter of the "Skywalker Saga".

12
00:58:45,517 --> 00:58:51,517
The film stars Ewan McGregor, Natalie Portman, Hayden
Christensen, Ian McDiarmid, Samuel L.

13
01:03:39,310 --> 01:03:45,310
Jackson, Christopher Lee, Anthony Daniels, Kenny Baker, and Frank Oz.

14
01:08:33,103 --> 01:08:39,103
The story is set ten years after The Phantom Menace, as thousands of planetary systems slowly secede from the Galactic
Republic and join the newly formed Confederacy of Independent Systems, led by former Jedi Master Count Dooku.

15
01:13:26,896 --> 01:13:32,896
With the galaxy on the brink of civil war, Obi-Wan Kenobi investigates a mysterious assassination attempt on Senator Padmé Amidala,
which leads him to uncover a clone army in service of the Republic and the truth behind the Separatist movement.

16
01:18:20,689 --> 01:18:26,689
Meanwhile, his apprentice Anakin Skywalker is assigned to protect
Amidala and develops a secret romance with her.

17
01:23:14,482 --> 01:23:20,482
Soon, the trio witness the onset of a new threat to the galaxy: the Clone Wars.

18
01:28:08,275 --> 01:28:14,275
Development of Attack of the Clones began in March 2000, some
months after the release of The Phantom Menace.

19
01:33:02,068 --> 01:33:08,068
By June 2000, Lucas and Hales completed a draft of the script, and
principal photography took place from June to September 2000.

20
01:37:55,862 --> 01:38:01,862
The film crew primarily shot at Fox Studios Australia in Sydney, with
additional footage filmed in Tunisia, Italy and Spain.

21
01:42:49,655 --> 01:42:55,655
It was one of the first motion pictures shot completely on
a high-definition digital 24-frame system.

22
01:47:43,448 --> 01:47:49,448
Attack of the Clones was released by 20th Century Fox
in the United States on May 16, 2002.

23
01:52:37,241 --> 01:52:43,241
It received mixed reviews from critics; the film's increased focus on action was
praised, while the characters and dialogue were regarded more critically.

24
01:57:31,034 --> 01:57:37,034
It performed well at the box office, making $653.8 million worldwide.

25
02:02:24,827 --> 02:02:30,827
Yet, it became the first Star Wars film to get outgrossed in its year of
release, becoming the fourth-highest-grossing film of 2002 worldwide.

26
02:07:18,620 --> 02:07:24,620
Revenge of the Sith (2005) followed Attack of the Clones,
concluding the Star Wars prequel trilogy.

27
02:12:12,413 --> 02:12:18,413
The film explores themes of army, laser gun, senate, investigation, sequel.

28
02:17:06,206 --> 02:17:12,206
The tone is thought_provoking.
